e an old  restaurant I mean sometimes you do  really find really old restaurants in  certain ski resorts we've been skiing  for quite a while here honestly skiing  in general is something that's really  old and it's an interesting conversation  because it's one of these things that  kind of started appearing all over the  world I think there are a lot of claims  that skiing came from Scandinavia or  from the Alps but in reality I think  it's probably from just about everywhere  and apparently the oldest claims of the  invention of skiing are actually from  China from thousands of years ago where  it used to be your hunting practice and  in general it's interesting how a skiing  is one of those sports that is really  based on hunting since in a snowy  environment it is really the best way to  get around even on flat ground or just  slightly hilly ground it's much more  efficient than walking around in deep  snow  so yeah that's not quite an accurate  history not quite a very detailed  history but just as far as I remember  the history of skiing it is really  really old and it's been done all over  the world  for a really long time it's just that  only in the recent century  it's become a sports on the scale that  we know today which I think is  particularly caused by the intervention  of ski lifts and easier ways to move  around and the fact that people have  gotten rich enough to afford free time  and to afford skiing at least some  people because at the end of the day  skiing is still something that really  only middle-class people or Richard can  afford and still very expensive and it's  getting more expensive and it's getting  more difficult because climate change  and all that so yeah it's not something  that everybody can participate in for  sure at least everybody can build ski  resorts in Planet Coast I suppose if  that's any consolidation anyway I'm  getting way off topic so I'm adding the  back of the building here and I put a  tweet out where I said that this has  been one of these buildings where I  accidentally make the back look better  than the front which is a bit of a  controversial statement maybe maybe you  don't agree with that but definitely  when I built the back I tried to keep it  less detailed than the front and a bit  more simple but at the end of the day I  thought it looked better than the front  especially with the mountains in the  back so yeah here it goes my favorite  part of this build actually the bank is  kept much more simple and traditional  and mostly just had windows in places  where I felt it would make sense for the  restaurant inside and then it has kind  of the back door on the sides where I  suppose you could supply stuff or  whatever there might be a road on the  back or something like that I'm not  entirely sure how I'm going to work all  of that out but what I do know is that I  feel like from the back it's a slightly  better building just a slightly better  composition a bit less over the top with  all of those glass facades and it just  looks a bit more rustic I feel but I  guess you can be the judge of that  after the cinematic shots at the end of  the video as well now it's finally time  to add details inside the umbrella bar  all this time there's been snow inside  which kind of doesn't make that much  sense so I'm adding an actual floor in  now and the way that I was doing this is  oops this looks like a bit of weird  imagery forget  that anyway the way that I did this is  rotating some wooden floors twice  actually and the second time kind of  sinking them just below the other ones  to avoid having z-fighting  the rotation trick to make domes and  round shapes and things like that is  really neat but you always have to watch  out with Si fighting because if you have  too many textures that are exactly at  the same height everything just starts  looking like a mess so that's why I  ended up doing it like that and then I'm  building a very simple bar in the middle  but there really isn't much to this I  probably could have added some crates or  whatever if they existed but I'm just  detailing this to the minimum extent  then I would have to make this look  believable from the outside it's not  really per se meant to be seen from  inside but I think with all of these  tools the custom little stools by the  way which are literally just a wooden  post and an art piece and also the the  tables and some of the bottles and the  basic bar it generally looks quite  believable from the outside I feel so  that's basically why I did that now I  did forget one thing and I was already  almost going to record this commentary  at this point but then I realized that I  didn't have any skis or other equipment  outside of these buildings and that  really doesn't make sense because if  you're going here then you'll probably  be arriving with skis or a snowboard or  whatever other equipment you used to go  down a mountain and you want to leave  them somewhere so you often find wrecks  of skis and snowboards just outside  these things I couldn't find any  snowboard racks so pretty much everybody  here is skiing but yeah that's something  that realistically I really had to add  to these buildings because it's such an  iconic part of these buildings as well  to think that they're just kind of  placed in a sea of skis everywhere and  the slightly annoying thing about this  was that I did want it to look realistic  enough in terms of colors so I went and  individually gave all of these skis at  color it's a bit random but yeah at  least they almost all have and have a  unique color so that's a neat little  detail there that I spent too much time  on but I think in the end if you look at  the whole thing and you can see all of  these weird colors everywhere it just  looks a bit more realistic than seeing  all kinds of skis with the same color  patterns and I'm also putting some  helmets and stuff outside not sure who  would leave their helmet outside but I  guess it's something you could do anyway  that's it for this episode thank you  guys for watching and I hope to see you  in the next one  [Music]  you
 

